  "note": "Compander sections. Philips NE570 product data (2003 Apr 03), Figs. 2, 6, 9 and 10: R1 10k from RECT IN to the VREF summing node; the rectified input current charges the CRECT pin, flows through R5 10k into the mirror input (diode-connected Q8) and is mirrored x2 to IG; R2 20k from G CELL IN to the cell's VREF summing node; the cell's output current IG*IIN/I1 (I1 = 140 uA) enters the op-amp's inverting summing node (INV IN); R3 20k from INV IN to the R3 pin, R4 30k from INV IN to GND; the op-amp's + input at VREF = 1.8 V above GND. The THD trim pin is not brought out (it sits at VREF).",
